<h2 class="frb-section-title center frb-text-center">Hoshizaki ice machine and fridge repair FAQs</h2>
<div class="frbx-faq" style="margin-top:36px"><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">Can you inspect a Hoshizaki ice machine that has stopped making ice?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>You can enquire about an independent service assessment for a Hoshizaki unit that has stopped producing ice. Have the model number, symptom, alarm information and location ready. Service suitability and timing need confirmation because ice-making systems vary and some repairs require specific tools or components.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">Why is my Hoshizaki ice maker producing smaller batches?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>Reduced production may involve operating temperature, ventilation, water flow, scale accumulation or a mechanical fault. Record whether output drops during hot periods or after heavy use. Follow the correct user manual for safe checks and arrange professional testing when the cause is unclear or production remains unreliable.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">What do flashing lights on a Hoshizaki KM machine mean?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>A flashing indicator may be a diagnostic alert, but its meaning depends on the exact Hoshizaki model and controller. Record the flash sequence and product code before asking for help. Do not bypass interlocks or repeatedly reset the machine. Technical documentation and on-site checks are needed for reliable interpretation.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">How often should a Hoshizaki ice machine be cleaned?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>Hoshizaki Australian guidance recommends that trained service personnel clean and sanitise an ice-maker water system at least twice yearly and check or clean the condenser at least annually. The precise instructions vary by model and operating conditions. A venue may need more frequent attention depending on its water supply and usage.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">Are you an authorised Hoshizaki repair agent?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>This page provides information about an independent commercial refrigeration service and does not claim official Hoshizaki authorisation. Check the manufacturer's support channel if the appliance is covered by warranty or an existing service agreement. You can then decide whether an independent assessment is appropriate for the fault.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">Can you help with a leaking Hoshizaki ice maker?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>A leaking ice maker should be kept clear of foot traffic and electrical hazards. Record where water emerges and whether it appears during filling, ice harvest or shutdown. A technician may need to inspect water lines, drainage and control operation. Do not dismantle plumbing or electrical components without proper qualifications.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">What should a café do when its ice machine fails?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>Stop relying on questionable ice and arrange a safe temporary supply from an appropriate source. Keep records of affected equipment and any hygiene concern. Note the model, current alarm and the change in output, then seek service. Ice used for drinks must remain safe for customers, not merely cold.</p></div></div><div class="frb-faq-item frb-reveal"><h3 class="frb-faq-question">How much does Hoshizaki ice machine repair cost?</h3><div class="frb-faq-answer"><p>Commercial repair cost varies with equipment type, diagnosis, site access, cleaning requirements and replacement parts. The website's from-$69 call-out information should not be assumed to cover every commercial machine or after-hours job. Ask the team to confirm attendance charges and provide a clear quote before repairs begin.</p></div></div></div></div></section>", "_css_classes": "frbw", "_title": "Hoshizaki - faq"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "b4d578b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "html", "isInner": false, "settings": {"html": "<section class="frb-cta-section"><div class="frb-container" style="padding:0">
